==Enemy==
This enemy has extremely long range and high damage. She has a somewhat long attack rate and attack animation, but she also has a chance to [[Weaken|weaken]] your cats to 10% of their normal attack power! Fortunately, she has slow speed and surprisingly, a high knockback count. When you first encounter her, it is highly recommended to collect '''ALL''' [[anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] up to that point so she is at a beatable difficulty level for the average player.

Unlike her variants [[Cruel Angel Clionel]], [[Death Angel Z-Onel]], [[Great Angel Chibinel]] and [[Marquis Clionius]], she doesn't have [[Long Distance]], and thus has no blind spot nor piercing range.

==Strategy==
Not many units can outrange Cli-One, so focus on Cats that can survive her attacks. Most [[Crazed Cats (origin)|Crazed Cats]] will be a big help, [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank]] in particular. [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer Cat]] is also useful against her, and the default [[Cat Cannon]] can interrupt her attacks. Overall, you should treat her like an upgraded, more advanced version of [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]].

She is easily knocked back by [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]], [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Warlock and Pierre]], [[Takeda Shingen (Uber Rare Cat)|Takeda Shingen]], [[Catman (Uber Rare Cat)|Catman]] and other units that can do extreme damage to her. [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Radiant Aphrodite]] is outranged, but can hit Cli-One with her [[Long Distance]], and [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]] fully outranges Cli-One, dealing good damage and knocking her back.

