==Trivia==
*Cli-One is based on [[wikipedia:Sea angel|sea angels]], sometimes called "cliones". She resembles the [[wikipedia:Clione limacina|common clione]] in particular.
**Cli-One's name may refer to how she is the first clione in [[The Battle Cats]] (i.e., Cli-One is clione number one) or to her being alone, unlike [[Cruel Angel Clionel]], [[Death Angel Z-Onel]] and [[Marquis Clionius]] who are joined by their kids.
**Cli-One and her full-sized variants' Japanese names all contain クオリネ ''kuorine'', an anagram of クリオネ ''kurione'' (clione).
*Her appearance and attack animation may have been inspired by the [[:Category:EVA Angel Enemies|Angels]] from ''[[wikipedia:Neon Genesis Evangelion|Neon Genesis Evangelion]]''. The description tends to be a reference to the Moon in the ''[[wikia:Evangelion:Evangelion: 1.0 You Are (Not) Alone|Rebuild of Evangelion]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s movies, where a part of the plot takes place.
*When opening her head to attack, her attack animation is similar to the aliens in the sci-fi horror manga ''[[wikipedia:Parasyte|Parasyte]]''.
*Cli-One's variants have some similarities shared with each other, but not with Cli-One herself. All of her variants have 4 knockbacks and Long Distance, and all of her full-sized variants also have 4 movement speed, 71f <sup>2.37s</sup> foreswing, 74f <sup>2.47s</sup> backswing and 0 time between attacks.
*Prior to [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]] [[Version 12.5 Update|12.5]], the [[Enemy Guide]] entries for Cli-One, [[Maawth]], [[I.M. Phace]] and [[Cosmic Cyclone]] listed their traits as "([[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]], [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]])" instead of "(Alien/Floating)".

